This folder is a modified copy of IQPopt (https://github.com/XanaduAI/iqpopt),
distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE in this folder).

Files changed by the authors of this repository:

- iqp_optimizer.py
  - The default precision is float32. Set IQPOPT_X64=1 for float64, the
    upstream default.
  - Expectation values are evaluated in memory-bounded chunks of samples.
  - A pairwise path is used for large circuits whose generators act on at most
    two visible qubits. Set IQPOPT_EXACT=1 to use the original path.
  - The ancilla register can be sampled conditioned on its value, with a given
    number of samples per branch.
- training.py
  - In the scan ("turbo") loop the parameter history is moved to host memory
    and only the monitored steps are kept.
  - The step index can be passed to the loss, and an optional callback reports
    loss components in the progress bar.
- utils.py
  - initialize_from_data has two new options, zero_two_body and noise_all. The
    defaults reproduce the original behaviour.
- gen_qml/iqp_methods.py
  - The default precision is float32 unless IQPOPT_X64=1.
  - The MMD loss functions accept the conditioning arguments condition_mask
    and condition_values and the argument ops_wires.
  - The visible operators are placed at their wires without a Python loop.

File added: _test_scan_chunk.py, a self-test of the chunked evaluation.

__init__.py, gen_qml/__init__.py, gen_qml/sample_methods.py and gen_qml/utils.py
are unchanged.
